## 5. Low-band test and first nonuniform band

### 5.1 Exact symbolic consistency witness

**PROVED-HERE.** The requested two-/three-band symbolic obstruction does not
occur. Set

```text
b1=b2=b3=b4=0,
h=pi^3(pi-gamma), B=pi(pi-gamma), z=pi-gamma,
Q=h^q+B,
P=h^e+gamma+2z=h^e+2pi-gamma,
c=-1,
```

and set every other chart coordinate to zero. This point obeys all three gauges
and all coefficient-space declarations. Exact differentiation gives

```text
J(B,2pi-gamma)=-gamma,
J(h,2pi-gamma)=pi^2(2pi-3gamma),
J(B,h)=-2h,

J(Q,P)=-gamma
       +q*pi^2(2pi-3gamma)*h^(q-1)
       -2e*h^e.
```

Thus the `h=0` target equation and every level `1,...,q-2=2t-1` hold. The
only residual levels are `h=2t` and `h=3t+1`. For any fixed low cutoff `H`,
the same point satisfies all levels `0,...,H` once `2t-1>=H`. It also satisfies
`h=0` together with any fixed number of highest levels for sufficiently large
`t`, because its defects remain at those two moving middle levels. Therefore
neither the bottom two/three bands nor a fixed two/three-high-band subsystem can
have a uniform unit certificate.

**CONTROL / SCOPE.** This is a point of a proper subsystem, not a pair with
`J=-gamma`, not a representative of the four-tuple, and not an attainment
claim. Its purpose is solely to prove consistency of the proposed fixed-band
test.

