+# K16 t=3 hostile replay gate
+
+Date: 2026-09-03
+
+Verdict: CONFIRMED for fixed `t=3`, scope exactly the gauged K=16 order-chart
+necessary superset for `(40,28; M2'=37; V2'=3; J=c*gamma)` on `c != 0`.
+The `t=4` replay is MEASURED-MODULAR only.
+
+## 0. Custody
+
+MEASURED. I parsed `xmodel/k16-t3-gate-gpt55-20260903.run.v2` with `awk`,
+paired its `charged_input_<i>_sha256=` and `charged_input_<i>_basename=`
+fields, wrote `/tmp/k16_t3_gate_manifest.sha256`, and ran `sha256sum -c`.
+All 11 frozen files in `/tmp/jc2-lane.rf6sMg/inputs` returned `OK`. This used
+the receipt fields; no hash digit was retyped.
+
+MEASURED. `which Singular` is `/usr/bin/Singular`. `Singular -v` reports
+Singular 4.3.2 for x86_64-Linux, build 4330, 2024-04-01. Macaulay2 is not on
+`PATH` as `M2` or `m2`.
+
+MEASURED. New drivers and outputs are confined to `box/k16t3-gate-20260903/`.
+This report is the only new `xmodel` report file. I did not edit ledgers, did
+not invoke `jc2-lean`, and did not read the prohibited in-progress lane reports.
+
+## 1. t=3 mechanical replay
+
+MEASURED. The gate copy
+`box/k16t3-gate-20260903/t3/t_order_system.py` has SHA-256
+`e115d576e850523f8796008d1b9d7899382cbac918ac2e74419207d9e7e7dc28`,
+matching the frozen charged input. Its line-level type is clear:
+`t_order_system.py:4-20` says the chart is a necessary superset and that a unit
+ideal on the `c != 0` component proves fixed-`t` nonexistence. Lines 67-72
+apply the three target gauges. Lines 109-117 divide only by monic `h` in `pi`,
+so no coefficient leader is inverted. Lines 170-205 extract `sat(I,c)` and run
+ring/type and empty/nonempty controls.
+
+MEASURED. Regenerated audit:
+
+```text
+tuple=(40,28;37,3), (e,q)=(10,7)
+Phi=(-1,3/10)
+filtration dimensions=[1,1,1,2,2,2,3,3,3,5]
+alpha=21 beta=10 h=4 c=1 -> unknowns=36
+h-adic powers=0..13; coefficient equations=51
+level histogram={0:7,1:6,2:6,3:6,4:5,5:5,6:5,7:2,8:2,9:2,10:2,11:1,12:1,13:1}
+parameter-degree histogram={1:1,2:6,3:23,4:21}
+deterministic h-adic reconstruction=True
+```
+
+MEASURED-MODULAR. The three regenerated finite-field inputs have the charged
+hashes:
+
+| field | input SHA-256 | wall / RSS | result |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| `GF(32003)` | `7414711be8a87bec7f5a9ea47943c7181199fb2912840ce633b0bf96ba5652c3` | 63.44 s / 61,936 KiB | `[1]` |
+| `GF(32009)` | `2ca5e0a18f9140bbea15a5e925c76cbacf2b6e35939ee73befc583381624b5dd` | 47.62 s / 61,536 KiB | `[1]` |
+| `GF(32027)` | `59d99caa2f34e17d086666f7d25dd6b6ebbcaa5326a98f54c2918c79bafaea63` | 49.85 s / 61,816 KiB | `[1]` |
+
+MEASURED. Each modular output prints `CONTROL_ACTUAL_PAIR_PASS`,
+`CONTROL_RING_PASS`, both saturation wrapper controls, `MAIN_EXTRACT_RING_PASS`,
+`MAIN_DONE basis_size= 1`, `MAIN_SATURATED_EMPTY`, and `G[1]=1`. All three
+stderr files are empty. These remain modular evidence only.
+
+## 2. First preprocessing pass
+
+AUDIT. `triangular_preprocess.py:4-17` states the method: when a current row is
+`f=a*x+b` with `a in Q*` and `x` absent from `b`, delete `f` and `x` and
+substitute `x=-b/a`. Lines 140-152 implement exactly that test: the coefficient
+is `diff(expr,x)`, it must be rational and nonzero, and the remainder must not
+contain `x`. Lines 177-215 choose such a row and verify that substitution kills
